  <string name="destination_about_tri">Tri Bratya is a group of rocks near Kumbel. One approach leads across the Kok Zhailau plateau. The rocks also feature on a longer hike through the Titov lakes and Kumbel.</string>
  <string name="destination_about_bao">Big Almaty Lake sits in a mountain basin in the Big Almaty Gorge. Its water changes colour with the season. The walking approach follows the road from the barrier towards the lake.</string>
  <string name="destination_about_butakovka">This is the Lower Butakovsky Waterfall, framed by rock walls. The gorge also contains an Upper Waterfall. The lower falls lie along the left tributary of the Butakovka; visiting both makes a considerably longer hike.</string>
  <string name="destination_about_kok">Kok Zhailau is a plateau between the Small and Big Almaty gorges. It overlooks Almaty. One approach starts near Prosveshchenets, and the Batareyka waterfall lies nearby.</string>
  <string name="destination_about_furmanov">The approach to Furmanov Peak climbs through the Kim Asar Gorge from the Medeu area. The well-known mountain swings stand along the way. A longer hike continues to Panorama Peak.</string>
  <string name="destination_about_shymbulak">Shymbulak lies above Medeu in the Small Almaty Gorge. The resort can be reached by cable car or on foot. It is also a starting point for further mountain ascents.</string>
  <string name="destination_about_tourist">Tourist Peak lies near Kosmostantsiya, the starting point of the described hike. The summit overlooks surrounding mountains, including Sovetov and Komsomol peaks. The route crosses high mountain terrain.</string>
